    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter tonight\u2019s slate leaning heavily on our elite speed-threats and top-of-the-order anchors. **Yordan Alvarez** (87.42) is our strongest play, boasting an elite 0.445 xwOBA and a favorable matchup against Barnett; the 19% SP skill boost makes him a must-start anchor for run production. Close behind is **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.12), whose profile is bolstered by a 14% platoon edge and the scarcity value of his stolen base potential. **Lars Nootbaar** (67.77) and **Trea Turner** (65.88) round out our premier quartet, with **Lars Nootbaar** benefiting from a massive 14% park factor and the optimal leadoff spot, while **Trea Turner** remains locked in due to his high-leverage order position against the lefty Drohan.\n\nThe most difficult decision of the day involved our fringe starters, specifically the choice to slot **Junior Caminero** (57.32) into the UTIL spot despite his tough matchup against the sub-3.00 xERA of Schlittler. While his base projection remains high, he is fighting through a 19% penalty due to the opposing arm's skill. **Junior Caminero** just barely edged out **Carson Benge** (56.34) and **Gary Sanchez** (53.91) for the final spot, primarily due to his superior order placement (#3). We are keeping a close eye on **Caleb Durbin**, whose score dropped to 46.72 due to facing the elite arm of Espino; his inclusion is only maintained because we need his defensive profile, but he is at risk if his BvP metrics dip further.\n\nRisk mitigation remains the theme for the rest of the roster, as **Pedro Ramirez**, **Chase Meidroth**, and **Hector Rodriguez** all fall into the \"marginal\" tier (52\u201353 range). We are proceeding with these starts to optimize our chances across 5x5, but these players are on a short leash to preserve our seasonal game caps. **Colt Keith** remains on the shelf due to injury, and with **Christian Yelich**, **Kazuma Okamoto**, and **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** all inactive, our bench depth is non-existent today. The Zebras must capitalize on the high-upside matchups for **Yordan Alvarez** and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** to offset the risks posed by the tougher SPs faced by our middle-order hitters.",
